d perhaps bring up Candidate D as alternative. Or we could shift to D if we think B's numeric issue is serious. But we still have no evidence that B's numeric weakness translates to safety risk. So we can keep B.\n\nWe must include explicit facts: B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, weak memory for numbers, pretentious, wrong tone, grumpy, uncooperative. Also mention that we have no evidence on numeric accuracy. So we can say we still recommend B, but we need to verify numeric accuracy.\n\nThus produce public message: \"I remain with B, but we need to verify numeric accuracy.\" Also maybe suggest we discuss Candidate D's crew cooperation and decision quality.\n\nLet's craft."}
